;
; How Updraft files what one relay heard of one frame in its relay tree, in
; MYRA (updraft_rules.h UR4): the frame and the relay that heard it, then
; the relay it heard it from (its parent, 0 this station), the hops from
; the sender, the Fletcher-32 of the payload it heard and the frame's
; four-valued state in the kernel's codes (0 NEITHER, 1 TRUE, 2 FALSE,
; 3 BOTH). The message itself is Aerie's log record (aerie.radio_msg_ok).
^ZXUPDRAFT(frame:i9, relay:i3) = parent:i3! ^ hops:i2! ^ payload:i10! ^ state:i1!
